seg-b3cacb309b66 = Grid timing: IEEE C37.118.2 PMU streams (library, MODELLED)

# text
# c1: kshana::c37118
# c2: STAT
# c3: FRACSEC
# c4: sync_losses
seg-89590cac5c20 = <c1/> reads a capture of synchrophasor frames (a TCP stream or a dump of UDP payloads) and reports each PMU's time health: the sync-error bit, the time-quality and unlocked-time classes in the <c2/> word, and the message time quality and leap-second flags in <c3/>. <c4/> groups consecutive sync-error reports into intervals. Every frame's CRC is checked. A data frame is read only after a configuration frame (CFG-2) has given each PMU's channel layout. Phasor values are stepped over, not decoded.

# text
# c1: kshana obs convert
# c2: kshana.obs/1
# c3: tests/c37118.rs
seg-bdbadd0ca1c1 = It is not yet a <c1/> reader, because the <c2/> schema has no field for time quality. That needs a schema minor version. It is checked against a stream from an independent encoder (<c3/>); no public PMU capture has been checked yet.

